{"name":"Candlelight","hex":"#fcd917","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"candlelight","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The light emitted by a candle.","The evening, when darkness falls and it is time to light candles."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/candlelight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Candle","blocks":[{"text":"A candle is an ignitable wick embedded in wax, or another flammable solid substance such as tallow, that provides light, and in some cases, a fragrance. A candle can also provide heat or a method of keeping time. Candles have been used for over two millennia around the world, and were a significant form of indoor lighting until the invention of other types of light sources. Although electric light has largely made candle use nonessential for illumination, candles are still commonly used for functional, symbolic and aesthetic purposes and in specific cultural and religious settings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/LA2_Skultuna_kontorsljusstake.jpg/330px-LA2_Skultuna_kontorsljusstake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candle","wikidata":"Q12888135"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Always.gif/330px-Always.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Always.gif/330px-Always.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The wick of a burning candle ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlways.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/LA2_Skultuna_kontorsljusstake.jpg/500px-LA2_Skultuna_kontorsljusstake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/LA2_Skultuna_kontorsljusstake.jpg/1280px-LA2_Skultu